bin/
obj/
/packages/
riderModule.iml
/_ReSharper.Caches/
**/.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.user

# Client-side libraries restored by LibMan from libman.json (bootstrap, aspnet-client-validation).
# Not committed; `dotnet libman restore` (or Rider/VS on build, or the Docker build stage)
# materialises them.
Homespool.Host/wwwroot/lib/

# Local-only working notes. No trailing slash on either: both are symlinks as of 2026-07-28, and a
# trailing slash matches a directory only - so it let the symlink show up as untracked, one
# `git add -A` from being committed.
AGENT-NOTES.md
notes

# Protocol captures / raw stream dumps (local reference only)
private-captures/

# Local compose secrets (SMTP password etc.) - never commit
# .env holds SMTP_PASSWORD and GO2RTC_PASSWORD and is the one file here with no commit behind it.
# The glob covers what setup-env.sh writes beside it (.env.backup-*) and whatever anybody moves aside
# by hand - .env.old and .env.bak were both committable while only the bare name was listed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Captured server output. Verbose logging carries fingerprints and printer identifiers, so these
# stay local even though they hold no credential outright (the registration code is deliberately
# never logged - see PrusaConnectService.GetPrinterCode).
logs/

# Self-signed cert/key generated by start-mailpit-tls.sh - private key material, local only
Homespool.Host.IntegrationTest/.mailpit-tls/

# SQLite database and its WAL sidecars (-wal, -shm, -journal). Never commit: once phase 1.5
**/*.Sqlite*
*.Sqlite*

# Claude Code's directory. AI tool configuration and personal instructions are not part of this
# project and should not reach anyone who self-hosts it, so the folder is ignored wholesale
# (Henrik, 2026-08-08) rather than named file by file - a question with no stable edge, which had
# already produced a second file nobody decided to add.
#
# launch.json stays tracked, and needs no exception rule: .gitignore governs untracked files only,
# so anything already in the index is unaffected. Deleting it from the index is what would remove
# it, and that is deliberately not done.
.claude/

# Firmware archives left here by separate work that happens to share this directory. Large
# binaries, and not build inputs of this project.
firmware/

# The rig container's /usb mount - whatever a test transfer downloaded. Scratch, and potentially
# large gcode.
rig/usb/

# The rig's enrolled identity: fingerprint plus the issued token. A credential.
#
# A glob, not the one filename, because one identity is one printer: a rig pretending to be a second
# machine needs a second file, and enrol.sh's OUT exists to write one. The exact-name form left
# rig/identity-xl.json and friends untracked-but-not-ignored, which is the state a `git add -A`
# commits - the same way api-token~ was committed on 2026-07-28.
rig/identity*.json

# The rig account's personal access token, written by enrol.sh. A credential, and one that acts as a
# whole user rather than a printer. The glob also covers editor backups
# (api-token~) - one of those was committed on 2026-07-28 by a `git add -A` and had to be amended out.
rig/api-token*

# Self-signed TLS material for printer-transport testing: CA key, server key, PFX, and the .der the
# printer trusts. Private keys - never committed.
rig/tls/

# The rig container's /internal/connect mount - the trust anchor connect_rig verifies against, and
# the private keys of whatever lab CA minted it. Deliberately separate from rig/tls/ above, which is
# stale material kept as a worked example and never to be reused: this one is minted fresh and
# expected to be thrown away after every database wipe.
rig/lab/

# Uploaded gcode. Runtime data, and the E2E tests leave some here when they exercise the upload
# endpoint against the real content root. See FileStorageOptions.
Homespool.Host/data/

# Scratch directory for pulling files off a printer's USB stick or a phone to look at them. Holds
# whatever was being debugged at the time - printer settings with credentials, photos of screens.
mitmattempt/

# Generated by pi/build.sh - container image tarballs and the built card image.
pi/work/

# Test results. Written by every test run (see Directory.Build.props) and pruned to the three
# most recent per project, so this holds recent evidence rather than an archive.
TestResults/
